# Repo-wide LFS backstop.
#
# urdf_viewer/.gitattributes and _slicer_branch/.gitattributes already track
# *.glb/*.gltf/*.obj (and a few app-specific patterns) for their own subtrees.
# This root-level file exists so any large binary asset added ANYWHERE in the
# repo -- including outside those two app trees, or before an app-specific
# .gitattributes is written -- is routed to Git LFS instead of landing as a
# regular Git blob. Deeper .gitattributes files still take precedence for the
# patterns they define; this is only a fallback for patterns they don't.
*.glb  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.gltf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.obj  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.stl  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp4  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
